`INSERT_IF_ABSENT` means “insert, or do nothing if the key already exists”. On the conflict path there is no modified row, so `getModifiedView()` cannot be relied on to contain the existing row’s database-generated id. “Save must never be followed by a query” is not a general Jimmer rule.

Smallest correct flow:

```java
@Transactional
public long createIfAbsent(ItemInput input) {
    SimpleSaveResult<Item> result = sqlClient
        .getEntities()
        .saveCommand(input)
        .setMode(SaveMode.INSERT_IF_ABSENT)
        .execute();

    Item item = result.getModifiedEntity();
    if (item != null) {
        return item.id();
    }

    return sqlClient
        .createQuery(ItemTable.$)
        .where(ItemTable.$.sku().eq(input.sku()))
        .select(ItemTable.$.id())
        .fetchOne();
}
```

