Configure Jimmer’s `CacheFactory`, not repository-level cache calls. Object/association caches are used transparently when Jimmer assembles entity graphs such as `Product` + `Category`.

```java
@Configuration
public class JimmerCacheConfig {

    @Bean
    public CacheFactory cacheFactory(
            RedisConnectionFactory redisConnectionFactory,
            ObjectMapper objectMapper
    ) {
        return new CacheFactory() {

            @Override
            public Cache<?, ?> createObjectCache(ImmutableType type) {
                if (type.getJavaClass() == Product.class ||
                    type.getJavaClass() == Category.class) {
                    return new ChainCacheBuilder<>()
                            .add(CaffeineBinder
                                    .forObject(type)
                                    .maximumSize(10_000)
                                    .duration(Duration.ofSeconds(30)))
                            .add(new RedisValueBinder<>(
                                    redisConnectionFactory,
                                    objectMapper,
                                    type,
                                    Duration.ofMinutes(30)
                            ))
                            .build();
                }
                return null;
            }

            @Override
            public Cache<?, ?> createAssociatedIdCache(ImmutableProp prop) {
                if (prop.getDeclaringType().getJavaClass() == Product.class &&
                    prop.getName().equals("category")) {
                    return new ChainCacheBuilder<>()
                            .add(CaffeineBinder
                                    .forProp(prop)
                                    .maximumSize(10_000)
                                    .duration(Duration.ofSeconds(30)))
                            .add(new RedisValueBinder<>(
                                    redisConnectionFactory,
                                    objectMapper,
                                    prop,
                                    Duration.ofMinutes(30)
                            ))
                            .build();
                }
                return null;
            }
        };
    }
}
```

Conceptually:

- `Product` object cache: `Product-id -> Product row`
- `Category` object cache: `Category-id -> Category row`
- association cache: `Product.category-productId -> categoryId`
- Caffeine is the fast local L1.
- Redis is the shared L2 across service instances.
- Repository methods still call Jimmer normally; no manual cache lookup per method.

After a Jimmer product update, the relevant cache entries must be invalidated, not patched manually:

- changed `Product` row ⇒ delete that product’s object-cache entry
- changed `product.category_id` / association ⇒ delete that product’s association-cache entry
- if the related `Category` row changes ⇒ delete that category’s object-cache entry
- other instances must receive the invalidation so their local Caffeine entries are also cleared

